    {
      "id": "s09",
      "type": "RECAP",
      "narration": "So, quickly. 0.1 plus 0.2 drifts because binary can't hold a tenth, so it rounds, and those rounding errors quietly add up.",
      "durationFrames": 294,
      "timingSource": "estimated",
      "background": "zoneC",
      "transition": "iris",
      "data": {
        "heading": "Why 0.1 + 0.2 drifts",
        "points": [
          {
            "text": "Binary can't store 0.1 exactly",
            "atWord": 8
          },
          {
            "text": "So the computer rounds it",
            "atWord": 15
          },
          {
            "text": "Rounding errors add up",
            "atWord": 18
